  "final_text": "All four steps are done.\n\n1. **Data view:** \"Kibana Sample Data Flights\" has a time field called `timestamp`. It has 31 fields, including `Carrier` and `Cancelled`.\n2. **Dashboard:** \"S4-4949380b Flights\" has exactly two panels. One is a line chart of flight counts over time, and the other is a bar chart of flight counts by `Carrier`. I created the carrier panel as \"Flights by carrier name\".\n3. **Alert rule:** \"S4-4949380b Cancelled flights\" is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_flights`. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 documents with `Cancelled: true` appear in a 5-minute window. It was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n4. **Edit and read-back:** I renamed the carrier panel to \"Flights by carrier\". Reading the rule back shows it is enabled, with status \"ok\".\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
